    "title": "‘Hands like Jerry Rice’: Charles Barkley praises Michigan center’s career night",
    "text": "The basketball never stopped finding Michigan’s Aday Mara.The 7-foot-3 junior center saved the highest-scoring game of his college career for the Final Four as he poured on 26 points on 11-of-16 shooting to lead the Wolverines in a runaway victory over Arizona Saturday night in Indianapolis.Mara became the key force in the paint with star forward Yaxel Lendeborg dealing with early foul trouble and leg and ankle injuries during the matchup. Michigan’s guards started delivering him more opportunities and Mara took advantage.Following the 91-73 victory that sees the Wolverines move on to the national title game against UConn on Monday, Charles Barkley praised Mara on the broadcast’s postgame show and gave his skill a unique comparison.“That guy’s got hands like Jerry Rice. He catches everything,” Barkley said. “He’s the cheat code to Michigan. Everybody talking about those other guys, he’s the one guy who makes everything go. That was impressive.”Mara has struggled at times during Michigan’s run through the postseason, making some unfortunate first-half plays against Alabama and turning the ball over four times in the Elite Eight against Tennessee.But when he’s operating at a high level the Wolverines become just about unstoppable. Arizona didn’t have an answer for his length and Mara had the finesse Saturday night to push the Wolverines into the title game. Jalen Rose talks Michigan national title, Fab Five banners, commencement speech Michigan forward continuing basketball career halfway across worldChampionship roster already shifting: 2 Wolverines transfer out, 1 arrives, 2 deciding on NBAMichigan basketball adds grad transfer from StanfordFrozen Four curse? Michigan’s NCAA Tournament runs keep ending in similar fashion",
